10	 * {@link OwnerIdentity identity key}) is already rejected by {@link EnsureUniqueIdentity}, so any
11	 * owner reaching this step has a key of its own. This step marks a softer, sound-alike collision:
12	 * an existing owner whose last name has the same {@link Soundex} code and whose postcode matches,
13	 * yet whose identity key differs (a different person who might be the same). It sets
14	 * {@code possibleDuplicate} to whether such an owner exists, with {@code possibleDuplicateOf} set
15	 * to that owner's id.
16	 *
17	 * <p>A declared household member ({@code sharesHousehold}) knowingly joins the household, so it is
18	 * not a suspected duplicate and stays {@code possibleDuplicate = false}. A blank postcode has
19	 * nothing to match on and is likewise left unflagged.
20	 *
21	 * <p>Runs after {@link AssignIdentityKey} has set the identity key and before {@link SaveOwner}
22	 * persists the entity, so {@code findAll()} sees only the owners that existed before this create.
23	 * The flags are stored on the owner and returned on every later read.
24	 */
25	public class FlagPossibleDuplicate {
26	
27	    public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
28	        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
29	        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
30	
31	        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
32	            return; // a declared household member is not a suspected duplicate
33	        }
34	        String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
35	        if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
36	            return;
37	        }
38	        String soundex = Soundex.encode(owner.getLastName());
39	        String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
40	        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
41	            if (existing.isDeleted()) {
42	                continue; // a soft-deleted owner no longer collides
43	            }
